@hostname = localhost
@port = 5033
@host = http://{{hostname}}:{{port}}

### 1. Get Active Users (Initial State)
# Expected: Returns Alice and Bob. Charlie is soft-deleted, so he is automatically filtered out.
GET {{host}}/api/users
Accept: application/json

### 2. Get All Users Including Deleted (Charlie is visible)
# Expected: Returns Alice, Bob, and Charlie (who has isDeleted: true and deletedAtUtc populated).
GET {{host}}/api/users/with-deleted
Accept: application/json

### 3. Create a New User
# Expected: Creates the user "David" in active state (isDeleted: false).
POST {{host}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "David Miller",
  "email": "david@example.com"
}

### 4. Soft Delete User "Bob" (ID 2)
# Expected: Deletes the user. Under the hood, SoftDeleteInterceptor intercepts and marks IsDeleted = true.
DELETE {{host}}/api/users/2

### 5. Get Active Users Again (Bob should be gone)
# Expected: Returns Alice and David. Bob and Charlie are filtered out.
GET {{host}}/api/users
Accept: application/json

### 6. Get All Users Including Deleted (Verify Bob's status)
# Expected: Returns Alice, Bob (isDeleted: true), Charlie (isDeleted: true), and David (isDeleted: false).
GET {{host}}/api/users/with-deleted
Accept: application/json

### 7. Restore Soft Deleted User "Bob" (ID 2)
# Expected: Bob is restored. IsDeleted is set to false and DeletedAtUtc is set to null.
POST {{host}}/api/users/2/restore

### 8. Get Active Users (Bob should be back!)
# Expected: Returns Alice, Bob, and David.
GET {{host}}/api/users
Accept: application/json
